-- title:
--   The public width of the prefix grows precisely on a set bit.
-- statement:
--   The public width of the prefix grows precisely on a set bit. In particular zero,
--   including the empty prefix, always has width one.
--
--   This lemma is part of OpenAI's machine-checked proof that rational linear programs can be solved by a strongly polynomial algorithm on a real-number RAM (Smale's ninth problem). It is used in the proof of `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.Compression.widthScanBlock_spec`.
